# Concurrency

- Every `std::atomic` operation states its memory order explicitly, with a comment justifying it. Never rely on the default `seq_cst` silently.
- Pad or align data written by different threads with `alignas(std::hardware_destructive_interference_size)` to avoid false sharing.
- No blocking locks in the job system's hot paths. A mutex is allowed only in setup/shutdown and must be commented.
- `wait()` must help by running other jobs, never spin-sleep idly.
- Any lock-free structure needs a stress test (many threads, millions of operations) before it's considered done.
- Document ownership: which thread may read or write each piece of shared data.
- When unsure whether code is race-free, say so explicitly instead of guessing.